            </note>
            <note corresp="#d823-f2" n="23" xml:id="d823-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg600">p. 600</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d823-f3" n="24" xml:id="d823-f3-content">
                <p>Lt. Gen. George H. Brett, Commanding General, Caribbean Defense Command.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d823-f4" n="25" xml:id="d823-f4-content">
                <p>Rear Adm. Howard F. Kingman, Commander, Panama Sea Frontier.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d823-f5" n="26" xml:id="d823-f5-content">
                <p>The Ambassador reported in his telegram 144, February 19, 1945, 5 p.m., that the
                    Ecuadoran Government was agreeable to beginning the conversations on the date
                    indicated (810.20 Defense/2–1945).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
